{"name":"Tamale","hex":"#f0e4c6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tamale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Ghana, the capital city of the Northern Region."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tamale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tamale","blocks":[{"text":"A tamale is a traditional Mesoamerican dish made of masa, a dough made from nixtamalized corn, which is steamed in a corn husk or banana leaves. The wrapping can either be discarded prior to eating or used as a plate. Tamales can be filled with meats, cheeses, fruits, vegetables, herbs, chilies, or any preparation according to taste, and both the filling and the cooking liquid may be seasoned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Tamal_oaxaque%C3%B1o.jpg/330px-Tamal_oaxaque%C3%B1o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamale","wikidata":"Q1147853"},{"title":"Tamale (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tamale\" is a hip-hop song by the American rapper and producer Tyler, the Creator, released as the seventeenth and penultimate track from his third studio album Wolf (2013). The song was solely written and produced by Tyler, the Creator, and was released with the rest of its parent album on April 2, 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Tamale_%28song%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamale_(song)","wikidata":"Q94014127"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tamales-florentine-codex.png/330px-Tamales-florentine-codex.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tamales-florentine-codex.png/330px-Tamales-florentine-codex.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tamales serve